From 9ed35742b65428be29cc4d8db8f1fda7fe9b4e09 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 16:59:09 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 09855/11362] [outer-loop] CI: decouple python-test from
 python-lint so the suite reports again

Operator directive: unskip CI's full-suite job.

python-test declared `needs: python-lint`. python-lint has been failing
continuously, so python-test returned SKIPPED -- not failed -- on every
recent run. Verified on run 32768818081: Python Lint & Type Check failure,
Python Tests (100% coverage) skipped. Skipped reads as "nothing to see" in
the UI, which is why nobody noticed the suite had stopped reporting.

This compounds a second gap. A 2026-04-14 commit abandoned the conductor's
own `run_tests(full=True)` branch on the grounds that "Full suite runs via
CI." That was false, or became false. Between the dead branch and the
skipped job, this project has had NO full-suite reporter anywhere, and the
only thing incidentally exercising the suite was a misplaced precondition
inside two experiment scripts -- itself removed earlier today for blocking a
model load on unrelated suite health.

Lint health and test health are independent signals. A formatting violation
should not hide whether 57,013 tests pass. Gating them together lets the
cheap signal silence the expensive one, which is what happened.

NOT fixing lint here, and the scale is why: 3,953 ruff errors, 5,437 files
needing reformat out of 9,432 in scope, and one blocking mypy error in the
vendored thrml tree. That is a diff across more than a third of the repo's
tracked Python, touching experiment scripts that are the research record,
including 223 unsafe-only fixes. It deserves its own change with nothing
else in it, not a side effect of unskipping a job. The drift accumulated
because pre-commit lints only CHANGED files while CI lints python/ tests/
wholesale, so every commit passes locally while the corpus rots.

Restore `needs: python-lint` once lint is green. The rationale is recorded
in the workflow itself so a future reader does not "tidy up" the missing
dependency.

NOT CHANGED, and still skipped: rust-test needs rust-check (also failing),
and spec-coverage needs [rust-test, python-test]. So spec-coverage stays
skipped until the Rust chain is addressed too. Out of scope here; flagged
rather than silently half-fixed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JntPrUGLNesPcJH1pyfFYw
---
 .github/workflows/ci.yml | 19 ++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/.github/workflows/ci.yml b/.github/workflows/ci.yml
index c6b16deafe..5dab10f3f6 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/ci.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/ci.yml
@@ -98,7 +98,24 @@ jobs:
   python-test:
     name: Python Tests (100% coverage)
     runs-on: ubuntu-latest
-    needs: python-lint
+    # DELIBERATELY NOT `needs: python-lint` (removed 2026-08-24).
+    #
+    # python-lint has been failing continuously, so this job returned SKIPPED
+    # rather than failed on every recent run. Skipped reads as "nothing to see"
+    # in the UI, so nobody noticed the suite had stopped reporting at all. A
+    # 2026-04-14 commit had already abandoned the conductor's own full-suite
+    # branch on the grounds that "Full suite runs via CI" -- which this made
+    # false. The project was left with no full-suite reporter anywhere.
+    #
+    # Lint health and test health are independent signals. A formatting
+    # violation should not hide whether 57,013 tests pass. Gating them together
+    # means the cheaper signal can silence the expensive one, which is exactly
+    # what happened.
+    #
+    # Restoring the dependency is fine ONCE lint is green. As of 2026-08-24 that
+    # is 3,953 ruff errors, 5,437 files needing reformatting, and one blocking
+    # mypy error in the vendored thrml tree -- deliberate work, not a side
+    # effect of this change. See ops/known-issues.md.
     steps:
       - uses: actions/checkout@v4
 
